# DevNet — Core Agent Rules

## Project nature

- **Developer community SPA** (Dev.to–style): posts, tags, auth, engagement, and an admin dashboard.
- **Not a monorepo / microservices app.** One Vite frontend talks to Supabase (Postgres + Auth + RLS).
- **Roles matter:** admin and moderator gates for `/admin`; keep RBAC and input sanitization (e.g. markdown/HTML) intact.
- **Primary overview:** `README.md`. There is no `docs/` product/requirements tree.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
| ------- | -------- |
| UI | React 18 + TypeScript + Vite 5 |
| Routing | `react-router-dom` v6 (`basename="/devnet"`) |
| Data | TanStack Query + `@supabase/supabase-js` |
| UI kit | shadcn/ui (Radix) + Tailwind CSS |
| Auth / DB | Supabase (`src/integrations/supabase/`, `supabase/migrations/`) |
| Deploy | GitHub Actions → static `dist/` on Nginx (`launch.giangnt.dev`, project `devnet`) |

Dev server: port **8080**. Production base path: **`/devnet/`** (see `vite.config.ts` and `App.tsx`).

## Repo layout

```
src/
  pages/           → Index, Auth, Write, Admin, AdminLogin, NotFound
  components/      → Layout, PostCard, ui/* (shadcn)
  contexts/        → AuthContext (Supabase session + admin check)
  hooks/           → shared React hooks
  integrations/supabase/ → client + generated types
  lib/             → utilities (e.g. cn)
public/            → static assets
supabase/          → config + SQL migrations
infra/nginx/       → modular + standalone Nginx templates
docs/              → DEPLOYMENT.md + deploy diagram
.github/workflows/ → build + deploy
```

Path alias: `@` → `src/`.

## Before changing behavior

| Area | Look here |
| ------ | ----------- |
| Features / setup | `README.md` |
| Routes / providers | `src/App.tsx`, `src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx` |
| Schema / RLS / roles | `supabase/migrations/*.sql`, `src/integrations/supabase/types.ts` |
| Supabase client | `src/integrations/supabase/client.ts` |
| Deploy / base path | `vite.config.ts`, `infra/nginx/`, `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`, `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md` |
| UI primitives | `src/components/ui/*` (prefer `shadcn` CLI when adding components) |

Prefer matching existing page/component patterns over inventing new layers.

## Scope discipline

- Minimize diff scope; match patterns in the touched area.
- Do not commit secrets or real Supabase keys in `.env` / client config.
- Do not add markdown/docs unless the user asks.
- Do not introduce a backend service, Prisma, or monorepo packages unless explicitly requested — Supabase is the backend.

## Diagrams

When asked for architecture, DB, or process diagrams, use the matching skill under `.agents/skills/`:

- `architecture-diagram`
- `db-schema-diagram`
- `process-flow-diagram`

## Token discipline

- Prefer `README.md` and the specific file you are changing over broad repo dumps.
- Open Supabase migrations/types only when schema, RLS, or role behavior is in scope.
- Do not assume Port-Vault / `docs/*` / `apps/*` / `services/*` layout — that is a different project.
